To convert a char to its ASCII value in Java, you can simply assign the character to an integer variable or explicitly typecast it to an int.Option 1: Implicit Typecasting (Recommended)Java automatically widens a 16-bit char into a 32-bit int, storing its corresponding numeric Unicode/ASCII code point.javachar character = 'A';
int asciiValue = character; // Automatically converts to 65

System.out.println("The ASCII value of " + character + " is: " + asciiValue);
Use code with caution.Option 2: Explicit TypecastingIf you need to display or use the value immediately within an inline operation (like System.out.println), use explicit typecasting. This is also considered highly readable.javachar character = 'a';

// Explicitly casting char to int returns 97
System.out.println((int) character); 
Use code with caution.Option 3: Extracting ASCII from a StringIf your character belongs to a String, extract it using the java.lang.String charAt() method before converting it to an integer:javaString text = "Java";
int asciiValue = text.charAt(0); // Fetches 'J' and converts to 74

System.out.println("ASCII value: " + asciiValue);
Use code with caution.Option 4: Convert an Entire String to an ASCII Byte ArrayIf you need to process an entire string and extract the ASCII values of all characters at once, convert the text directly into a byte array via java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets:javaimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String word = "ABC";
        byte[] asciiBytes = word.getBytes(StandardCharsets.US_ASCII);
        
        // Prints [65, 66, 67]
        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(asciiBytes)); 
    }
}
Use code with caution.Note: Standard ASCII ranges from 0 to 127. Because Java natively uses the Unicode character set (a backward-compatible superset of ASCII), any basic alphanumeric English character will perfectly match standard ASCII values.I'll tailor my next response. Just tell me:String or primitive char inputLooping or single character conversionTarget output data type neededJust reply with your answer or a new query to continue:


